---
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Logo from '../components/Logo.astro';
import { BRAND_NAME, COMPANY_ADDRESS, COMPANY_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, GOVERNING_COUNTRY } from '../consts';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';

const effective = 'November 7, 2026';
---

<Base
	title={`Terms of Use — ${BRAND_NAME}`}
	description={`The rules for using ${BRAND_NAME}: your photos, AI try-ons, shops and prices, try-on packs, and our responsibilities.`}
>
	<header class="container top">
		<Logo />
	</header>

	<main class="container policy">
		<h1>Terms of Use</h1>
		<p class="effective">Effective {effective}</p>

		<section class="summary" aria-labelledby="summary-title">
			<h2 id="summary-title">The short version</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>{BRAND_NAME} is for people 18 and older.</strong></li>
				<li>
					<strong>Only add photos of yourself,</strong> and nothing sexual, violent or
					illegal.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Try-ons are AI pictures,</strong> not a promise of how a piece will fit.
					Check sizes with the shop.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>We don’t sell anything except try-ons.</strong> You buy pieces from the
					shops, under their terms and prices.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Try-ons don’t expire and have no cash value.</strong> A failed try-on is
					refunded automatically, and refunds for purchases go through Apple.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<h2>Who we are and this agreement</h2>
		<p>
			{BRAND_NAME} is an AI stylist and fitting room for iPhone, run by {
				COMPANY_NAME ? COMPANY_NAME : <mark>[company or full legal name]</mark>
			}, {COMPANY_ADDRESS ? COMPANY_ADDRESS : <mark>[postal address]</mark>} (“we” or “us”).
			These terms are an agreement between you and us for using the app. By using {BRAND_NAME},
			you agree to them. How we handle your data is explained in our <a
				href={withBase('privacy/')}>Privacy Policy</a
			>.
		</p>

		<h2>Who can use {BRAND_NAME}</h2>
		<p>
			You must be 18 or older, and you confirm that when you add a photo. You need an Apple
			account to sign in, and you’re responsible for what happens under your account. Use
			{BRAND_NAME} only for yourself, not on behalf of a business.
		</p>

		<h2>Your photos and briefs</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Only add photos of yourself.</strong> Don’t add photos of other people, even
				with their permission, and never photos of anyone under 18.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Don’t add or ask for</strong> nudity, sexual content, violence, hate, or
				anything illegal or that you don’t have the right to use.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>You keep the rights to your photos and briefs.</strong> You let us process
				them, and send them to the AI providers named in our Privacy Policy, only to style
				your looks and make your try-ons.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			We may refuse a request that seems to break these rules. We don’t make try-ons of
			underwear or swimwear.
		</p>

		<h2>AI looks and try-ons</h2>
		<p>
			Looks and try-ons are made by AI. A try-on is an illustration: it can get the fit,
			colour, size or details of a piece wrong, and it can change how you look. The
			stylist’s suggestions are ideas, not professional advice. Check sizes, materials and
			fit with the shop before you buy.
		</p>
		<p>
			You can keep and share your try-ons for personal use. Don’t present them as real
			photos, or use them to mislead, harass or impersonate anyone. Try-ons are labelled as
			AI-generated, and Google adds an invisible SynthID watermark. Please don’t remove
			either.
		</p>

		<h2>Shops, products and prices</h2>
		<p>
			{BRAND_NAME} finds products from other shops through Google Shopping. We don’t sell
			these products, and we’re not part of your purchase. When you tap Buy, the shop’s own
			terms, prices, delivery and returns apply, and any questions about an order go to
			the shop.
		</p>
		<p>
			Prices, sizes and availability come from the shops and Google, and can be out of date
			or wrong. The price in the shop is the one that counts. In the future, some links may
			earn us a commission when you buy, at no extra cost to you.
		</p>

		<h2>Try-ons and payments</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Packs:</strong> you can buy packs of try-ons in the app. Apple takes the
				payment, under Apple’s terms. New accounts get a few try-ons free.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Using them:</strong> each try-on uses one. If a try-on fails, it’s refunded
				to your balance automatically. If a finished try-on comes out wrong, you can redo it
				once for free.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>What they are:</strong> try-ons don’t expire, but they have no cash value and
				can’t be transferred, exchanged or sold. Unused try-ons are lost when you delete your
				account.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Refunds:</strong> ask Apple for a refund of a purchase at
				<a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>. If Apple
				refunds a pack, we remove the try-ons it gave you.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Try-ons are delivered as soon as you buy them. If you’re in the EU or UK, you agree to
			that, and you understand that you then lose the 14-day right to cancel. This doesn’t
			affect refunds you can get from Apple or your other legal rights.
		</p>

		<h2>Fair use</h2>
		<p>Don’t:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Copy, scrape or resell {BRAND_NAME}, its looks or its results.</li>
			<li>Get around daily limits, the safety checks or the try-on balance.</li>
			<li>Reverse-engineer the app, or overload or attack our servers.</li>
			<li>Use {BRAND_NAME} to break the law or anyone’s rights.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			To keep the service working for everyone, we limit how many briefs and try-ons an
			account can run each day.
		</p>

		<h2>Suspending or closing an account</h2>
		<p>
			You can delete your account at any time in the Me tab. We may suspend or close an
			account that seriously or repeatedly breaks these terms, after telling you why where we
			can. If we close an account without a good reason, or stop offering {BRAND_NAME}, we’ll
			refund unused try-ons you paid for.
		</p>

		<h2>Our responsibilities</h2>
		<p>
			We work to keep {BRAND_NAME} running and its results useful, but the app is provided “as
			is”. It may be unavailable at times, AI results may be wrong, and features may change.
		</p>
		<p>
			We’re not responsible for products, shops, prices or orders, or for losses we couldn’t
			reasonably foresee. Where the law allows, our total liability to you is limited to what
			you paid us in the 12 months before the claim. None of this limits liability that can’t
			be limited by law, such as for death or injury caused by negligence, fraud, or gross
			negligence. If you’re a consumer in the EU or UK, you keep all the rights your local law
			gives you.
		</p>

		<h2>Apple</h2>
		<p>
			These terms are between you and us, not Apple, and we’re responsible for {BRAND_NAME}, not
			Apple. Apple has no obligation to maintain or support the app. If {BRAND_NAME} fails to
			meet a warranty that applies, you can tell Apple, and Apple will refund the price you
			paid for the app, if any. Apple has no other warranty obligation for it.
		</p>
		<p>
			We, not Apple, handle any claims about {BRAND_NAME}, including product liability, legal
			or regulatory requirements, consumer protection, and claims that the app infringes
			someone’s intellectual property. You confirm that you’re not in a country subject to a
			US embargo, and not on a US list of prohibited or restricted parties. Apple and its
			subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these terms and can enforce them against
			you.
		</p>

		<h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
		<p>
			If these terms change, we’ll update this page and the date at the top. If a change is
			significant, we’ll tell you in the app before it takes effect. Using {BRAND_NAME} after
			that means you accept the new terms. If you don’t, you can delete your account.
		</p>

		<h2>Law and disputes</h2>
		<p>
			These terms are governed by the law of {
				GOVERNING_COUNTRY ? GOVERNING_COUNTRY : <mark>[country]</mark>
			}. If you’re a consumer, you also keep the protection of the law where you live, and you
			can bring a claim in your local courts. Please contact us first, and we’ll try to sort it
			out.
		</p>

		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>
			Questions about these terms? Email us at {
				CONTACT_EMAIL ? (
					<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
				) : (
					<mark>[contact email]</mark>
				)
			}.
		</p>
	</main>

	<Footer />
</Base>

<style>
	.top,
	.policy {
		max-width: 46rem;
	}

	.top {
		padding-block: 1.5rem;
	}

	.policy {
		padding-block: clamp(1.5rem, 6vw, 3rem) clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem);
	}

	h1 {
		font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 3.5rem);
	}

	.effective {
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
		font-size: 0.9375rem;
	}

	h2 {
		margin-top: 3rem;
		font-size: 1.625rem;
	}

	p,
	ul {
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}

	p,
	li {
		color: var(--muted);
	}

	strong {
		color: var(--text);
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	ul {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
	}

	.policy a {
		text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
	}

	mark {
		padding-inline: 0.25em;
		border-radius: 0.25em;
		background: #f6d776;
		color: #212121;
	}

	.summary {
		margin-top: 2rem;
		padding: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2rem);
		background: var(--surface);
		border: 1px solid var(--line);
		border-radius: var(--radius-card);
	}

	.summary h2 {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
</style>
